# README - First Duplicate Element

## Aim
This folder contains programs to find the first duplicate element in an array using two different approaches.

---

## Algorithm
1. Read the array size and elements.
2. For the brute-force version, compare each element with all previous elements.
3. For the mapping version, store the index of each element in a hash map and check for mismatch.

---

## How it works
The brute-force method checks every pair of elements to detect a duplicate, while the mapping method uses a dictionary-like structure to track positions efficiently.

---

## Functionality
- Finds the first duplicated value in the array
- Prints the position of the duplicate if found
- Prints -1 if no duplicate exists

---

## Time and Space Complexity
- Brute-force version: Time O(n^2), Space O(1)
- Mapping version: Time O(n), Space O(n)
